{%- import "macros.njk" as m with context -%}
{%- set first = history.years | first -%}
{%- set latest = history.years | last -%}
<h1>State Pension history: rates and increases since 2010</h1>

{#- The years since the triple lock was first applied in which the published increase was not the one the rule gives, the highest of prices, earnings and 2.5%: worked out from the record, not typed. The lede needs at least one. -#}
{%- set departures = [] -%}
{%- for year in history.years %}{% if year.measure != "pre-triple-lock" %}{% set rule = 25 %}{% if year.prices_tenths > rule %}{% set rule = year.prices_tenths %}{% endif %}{% if year.earnings_tenths > rule %}{% set rule = year.earnings_tenths %}{% endif %}{% if year.applied_tenths != rule %}{% set _ = departures.push(year.tax_year) %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- if departures.length == 0 %}{{ "the history lede expects at least one year whose increase was not what the triple lock gives" | fail }}{% endif -%}
<p class="lede">The full rates of the State Pension have risen every April since the triple lock was first applied in April 2011, and in every year except {% if departures.length == 1 %}{{ departures[0] }}{% else %}{{ departures.slice(0, -1) | join(", ") }} and {{ departures | last }}{% endif %} the increase was the one the rule gives: the highest of prices, earnings and 2.5%. This page records every rate and decision from {{ first.tax_year }} to {{ latest.tax_year }} and marks the exceptions. The <a href="/tools/history/">history explorer</a> draws the rates and can calculate what another rule would have produced.</p>

